       "children": [
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "p",
         "text": "Why it matters",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Does a Good Graphic Designer Do for a Small Business?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A good graphic designer turns your message into something people notice and understand in a few seconds. For a flyer that means one clear headline, a reason to act and a phone number that is easy to find. For a banner at a Zilker event or a menu board on South Lamar, it means type that reads from across the room.</p><p>The other half of the job is technical. Printers need correct bleed, color mode and resolution; social platforms need exact pixel sizes. We handle those details so the file you send to the print shop or upload to Instagram looks exactly like the proof you approved.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "A clear visual hierarchy: headline, offer, call to action",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Consistent colors and fonts across every piece",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Files set up correctly for your printer or platform",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
