   "bg": "white",
   "variant": "generic",
   "children": [
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "p",
     "text": "Local answers",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "h2",
     "text": "Where Can I Find a Graphic Designer in Austin?",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "html": "<p>Logo Design Austin provides graphic design for businesses across Austin and the surrounding suburbs, fully online. You share your content by text or email, review proofs on your phone and get files you can send straight to any Austin print shop or upload to your social accounts.</p><h3>Event, restaurant and retail graphics for Downtown (78701), East Austin (78702) and South Congress (78704)</h3><p>Venues, bars, food trucks and boutiques need a steady stream of flyers, menus and social posts. We keep your look consistent from one promotion to the next, so regulars recognize you instantly.</p><h3>Real estate and home service marketing in Round Rock (78664), Cedar Park (78613) and Pflugerville (78660)</h3><p>Agents, contractors and cleaning companies rely on postcards, door hangers and yard signs. We design them with a clear offer and an easy-to-read phone number.</p><h3>Startup and tech graphics near the Domain (78758) and Mueller (78723)</h3><p>Young companies need pitch-deck graphics, event banners and launch visuals that look polished without a long agency process.</p><h3>Can you design my graphics if you did not design my logo?</h3><p>Yes. Send us your current logo files. If you only have a low-quality image, we can clean it up first so your printed pieces stay sharp.</p><h3>What should I send for a flyer or business card?</h3><p>Your logo file, the exact wording, any photos you want to use, the finished size and where it will be printed or posted. If you are not sure about wording, send rough notes and a designer will help you tighten the headline and the call to action.</p>",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
